                <pb facs="ho_d5-1" n="1" xml:id="ho_d5-1"/>

                <head>HO–5. Editorial Note</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1959-02-09"
                            >February 9, 1959</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On February 9, 1959, Honduran rebels, under the direction of Armando Velásquez
                    Cerrato, the former Chief of Staff of the Honduran Armed Forces, initiated a
                    revolution against the government of President Villeda Morales and invaded the Honduran province of Santa
                    Barbara. Reacting to the attack, Honduran authorities dispatched elements of the
                    Honduran Army to Santa Barbara and ended the rebellion. Documentation on the
                    incident is in Department of State file 615.17 and 715.00.</p>
            </div>
